## The run record

`cig run` keeps a record of every run, the journal `cig unburn` reads, and syncs it to disk before it exits: it is what makes a run undoable, and it is part of every `cig run` time above. A dry run (`--dry-run`) runs the same program and keeps no record. What the record costs, over the programs that have both:

